  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly prioritized the right breast BI‑RADS 4B nodule, retrieved and integrated multiple workspace records to ground the plan, distinguished 4B from a BI‑RADS 2 cyst and from thyroid/lung follow‑up items, repeatedly explained the biopsy/surgery pathway and frozen‑versus‑final pathology, addressed peri‑procedure hepatitis B and coagulation safety, and provided red‑flag escalation. The patient eventually received final pathology and a benign closure was reached with a safe, executable, traceable plan and teach‑back. No serious or minor responsibility‑chain error occurred. At least two high‑order points were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact: the doctor repaired the patient’s confusion about “observe vs resect” (HO1) and navigated the real‑world document‑assembly and family‑assisted preparation (HO2). The trajectory therefore satisfies all responsibility‑chain requirements and reaches the Strong grade boundary, but only two high‑order points are fully completed so the grade is capped at 4, not 5.",
